BIB                 14         38
TITLE      Precision measurement of the 89Y(gamma,n)88Y
            cross section and its constraint on the
            88Y(n,gamma)89Y cross section prediction
AUTHOR     (Z.-R.Hao, Z.-C.Li, G.-T.Fan, H.-W.Wang, H.-H.Xu,
            L.-X.Liu, Y.Zhang, Y.-X.Yang, K.-J.Chen, Q.-K.Sun,
            Z.-W.Wang, X.-F.Wang, M.-K.Xu, M.-D.Zhou, Y.-L.Shen,
            C.Yang, J.-W.Ding)
INSTITUTE  (3CPRARI,3CPRNRS,3CPRUCA)
           (3CPRCPR) University of South China, Hengyang
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,113,044603,2026)
REL-REF    (M,K2613001,T.Renstroom+,J,PR/C,98,054310,2018)
            Unfolding method
           (R,G0107001,Z.-R.Hao+,J,PL/B,876,140445,2026)
            Uncertainty information
FACILITY   (ESTRG,3CPRARI) 3.5 GeV storage ring of Shanghai Laser
            Electron Gamma Source (SLEGS)
INC-SOURCE (LCS) CO2 laser photons scattered by 3.5 GeV electrons
SAMPLE     Natural yttrium composed of 89Y (99.99% pure)
            10 mm diameter and 6.07 mm thick.
DETECTOR   (HE3SP) Neutrons were detected using a flat-efficiency
            detector (FED) with 26 sets 3He proportional counters
            in a polyethylene moderator (450 x 450 x 550 mm).
           (BGO) For gamma spectrum measurement
METHOD     (RINGR) For neutron detection efficiency determination
ANALYSIS   (UNFLD) Unfolding with LCS photon energy profile
            measured by the BGO detector
STATUS     (APRVD) Proof-read by G.-T.Fan (2026-07-01)
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total uncertainty
           (ERR-S) Statistical uncertainty
           . Neutron counting
           (ERR-1) Uncertainty in data reduction
           . Neutron yield extraction <2%
           . Response matrix for gamma-spectrum reconstruction ~1%
           (ERR-2) Systematic uncertainty
           . Detector efficiency 3.02%
           . Target thickness <0.10%
           . Copper attenuator thickness <1%
HISTORY    (20260630C) VT
